==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-UTC.ogg|a=Mid-Atlantic US}}

===Etymology 1===
A compromise {{l|en|initialism}} between English ''CUT'' (“Coordinated Universal Time”) and French ''TUC'' (“{{lang|fr|Temps Universel Coordonné}}”), unofficially giving “'''U'''niversal '''T'''ime '''C'''oordinated” and “{{lang|fr|'''U'''niversel '''T'''emps '''C'''oordonné}}”.

====Proper noun====
{{en-proper noun}}

# [[Coordinated Universal Time]], which is the international standard for [[civil time]] and the Internet.
#: {{syn|en|GMT}}

